// A submodule of left, which does NOT inherit left's neighbourhood.
//
// The registry is rebuilt at each level rather than accumulating as you descend:
// here it is left's namespace -- deep's own sisters, and what left published --
// so right is out of reach, because right is a sister of left and not of deep.
// left's import of right bound right's name in left privately, so even an
// import of it here would be refused. Written 'pub import right', it would be a
// public name of left, and 'import right;' here would bind it as any public name
// of the parent is bound (module-import-parent) -- but a bare name never climbs
// without that import.
//
// A module here that needs right says so to left, and left re-exports what it
// needs. That is the boundary doing its job, and it is what keeps this module
// liftable: its dependencies are stated at its own 'mod'.

mod deep;

fn tryReach(n i64) i64 {
  right.shown(n);           //~ ErrorUnkName "does not refer to a declared name"
}
